{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>The tithe of your grain, your wine, and your oil.</b> If you tithe properly, it is yours — your grain, your wine. But if not, it is Mine — My grain and My wine, as it is said: ״לכן אשוב ולקחתי דגני בעתו ותירושי במועדו״. And further, come and see how great is the power of tithes: in all the Torah it is written ״לא תנסו את ה' אלהיכם״, but regarding tithe it is written ״הביאו את המעשר אל בית האוצר ובחנוני נא בזאת וגו״. And our Rabbis, may their memory be blessed, interpreted: What is ״עד בלי די״? Until your lips wear out from saying ״די״."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:00:59.953614952Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}